@(A.236 = 236-239) A third time they threw fish spawn (?) into the river. The sorcerer made a cow and its calf  @varh[t1824.v25]{come out } @vart[t1824.v26,t1824.v25]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} arise } from the water. Wise Woman @wPN{Saŋburu}, however, made a lion  @varh[t1824.v27]{come out } @vart[t1824.v28,t1824.v27]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} arise } from the water. The lion seized the cow and its calf and  @varh[t1824.v29]{took } @vart[t1824.v30,t1824.v29]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} dragged } them to the reedbeds.

