@(A.249 = 249-254) Wise Woman @wPN{Saŋburu} said to him: @q[Sajburu,Ur-jiri-nuna]{“Sorcerer, you do have magical powers, but where is your sense? How on earth could you think of going to do sorcery at @wSN{Ereš}, which is the city of @wDN{Nisaba}, a city whose destiny was decreed by @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil}, the primeval city, the beloved city of @wDN{Ninlil}?”}

@(A.255 = 255-263) The sorcerer answered her: @q[Ur-jiri-nuna,Sajburu]{“I went there without knowing all about this. I acknowledge your superiority -- please do not be bitter.”} He pleaded, he prayed to her: @q[Ur-jiri-nuna,Sajburu]{“Set me free, my sister; set me free. Let me go in peace to my city. Let me return safely to @wSN{Aratta}, the mount of the lustrous @fsux{me}. I will  @varh[t1824.v37]{make known }@vart[t1824.v38,t1824.v37]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} declare } your greatness in all the lands. I will sing your praise in @wSN{Aratta}, the mount of the lustrous me.”}

